	(text "Odd pins left, even pins right.\nPin 26, CE1, stays open for a second\nSPI device. GPIO 12, 13, 20, 21 stay open.\nGPIO 19 is TFT_BL, the only pin that is\nnot a software default.\nPin map and net names: spec/pins.yaml.\nThe pin check compares this sheet with it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5ab6c529-2a22-5736-bf8e-8d7a5ce6cc20")
	)
	(wire
		(pts
			(xy 71.12 119.38) (xy 71.12 121.92)
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(uuid "b734d1ac-6c16-5178-b4bc-bf4a0908e8ba")
	)
	(wire
		(pts
			(xy 83.82 119.38) (xy 83.82 121.92)
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(uuid "894879ff-b008-5654-be32-6f223101dc61")
	)
	(wire
		(pts
			(xy 96.52 129.54) (xy 96.52 127)
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(uuid "ba5de524-3cb0-5f7d-9627-472a8d0c0264")
	)
	(text "The Pi feeds +3V3 and GND. +5V comes from\nthe Pi's USB port or from J3, never both."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6703ce9b-6cad-5695-8310-d9d258175726")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 12.7 149.86)
		(end 106.68 185.42)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "6afbc796-e1dc-577c-aa6a-0bd5c677adc7")
	)
	(text "For the board step: J1 side and pin 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 149.225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.3333)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ffdb9636-2e5f-5154-82c9-e3717fea3bed")
	)
	(text "1. J1's body sits on the BOTTOM face of this board.\n   The Pi Zero hangs below, its own parts facing up,\n   its male header pushed up into J1.\n2. That is the stacking of a normal HAT. Seen from\n   above this board, J1 pin 1 sits straight over the\n   Pi's pin 1. Do not mirror it a second time.\n3. In KiCad, J1 goes on the bottom layer, which\n   flips its pads. Move it so pad 1, seen from the\n   top, lands on the Pi's pin 1 in a top view.\n4. Prove it before placing anything else: lay the\n   Zero's footprint or drawing, top view, under J1\n   and match pin 1 and pin 2 to J1 pads 1 and 2.\nH5 to H8 sit at the Zero's M2.5 holes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "670bf349-40bb-53e3-b80d-8ff620c91a3e")
	)
